# Part in Friendship: "Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, ..." Turn 2: Bot2's own Ornithopter dies to its own Bolt: not
# a creature Bot1 controls, nothing. Turn 3: Lingering Souls makes two Spirit tokens. Turn 4: Bot2's Bolt kills a Spirit token:
# a token is no nontoken creature, nothing (the library keeps its count). Then a Bolt kills Bot1's Ornithopter and it triggers
# (the earlier token's death did not use up "once each turn"): the library has no creature card, so all of it is revealed and
# put back on the bottom in a random order - 15 cards before and after, all of them revealed (and none before).

